---
import './design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from './SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from './SketchArrow.astro';
---
<figure id="schema-anatomy" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface schema-anatomy wide" aria-labelledby="schema-anatomy-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Schema and data</span>
  <h3 id="schema-anatomy-title">The structure and the records it holds</h3>
  <div class="anatomy-layout">
    <section class="schema-panel" aria-labelledby="schema-declaration-title">
      <h4 id="schema-declaration-title">Schema</h4>
      <p class="panel-note">The table’s definition</p>
      <SketchSheet class="definition" tone="blue">
        <div class="table-name"><span>Table</span><strong>customers</strong></div>
        <div class="field key-field"><strong>customer_id</strong><span>text</span><small>Primary key · identifies each row</small></div>
        <div class="field"><strong>name</strong><span>text</span><small>A name must be supplied</small></div>
      </SketchSheet>
    </section>
    <div class="structure-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><SketchArrow /><span>Each row follows<br />this definition</span></div>
    <section class="data-panel" aria-labelledby="schema-records-title">
      <h4 id="schema-records-title">Data</h4>
      <p class="panel-note">Two records in <code>customers</code></p>
      <SketchSheet tone="teal"><table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col" class="key-column">customer_id</th><th scope="col">name</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody><tr><th scope="row" class="key-column"><code>C4</code></th><td>Ada</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="key-column"><code>C5</code></th><td>Ben</td></tr></tbody>
      </table></SketchSheet>
      <div class="row-bracket"><span aria-hidden="true">└</span><p>Another customer adds a row.<br />It doesn’t add another column.</p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <figcaption>The schema names the table and its columns, chooses their types and declares rules. The data supplies values for those columns. A primary key cannot be missing or repeated; names can repeat. This drawing shows one table in a larger schema.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .schema-anatomy.wide { margin-left:50%; }
  .anatomy-layout { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 6rem minmax(0,1fr); gap:1rem; margin:1.5rem 0; }
  .anatomy-layout section { min-width:0; margin:0; }
  .anatomy-layout h4 { font-size:1rem; margin:0; }
  .panel-note { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.8rem; margin:.15rem 0 1rem; }
  .table-name { display:flex; gap:.7rem; padding:.7rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .table-name span { color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .field { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto; padding:.7rem; gap:.2rem .4rem; }
  .field + .field { border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
  .field strong { font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  .field > span { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .field small { grid-column:1 / -1; font-size:.75rem; }
  .key-field,.key-column { background:var(--paper-match); }
  .key-field { box-shadow:inset 3px 0 var(--teal); }
  .structure-arrow { display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; gap:.6rem; text-align:center; font-size:.7rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .structure-arrow svg { display:block; width:100%; height:30px; color:var(--teal); }
  .structure-arrow path { fill:none; stroke:currentColor; stroke-width:1.5; stroke-linecap:round; stroke-linejoin:round; }
  .data-panel table { border-top:0; }
  .data-panel tbody th,.data-panel td { padding:.95rem .5rem; }
  .row-bracket { display:flex; gap:.5rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); padding-left:.5rem; }
  .row-bracket > span { color:var(--teal); font:2rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); }
  .row-bracket p { font-size:.75rem; }
  @media(max-width:680px) {
    .anatomy-layout { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); gap:.8rem; }
    .structure-arrow { flex-direction:row; align-items:center; justify-content:flex-start; text-align:left; gap:1rem; padding-left:1rem; }
    .structure-arrow :global(svg) { width:2.5rem; height:3rem; transform:rotate(90deg); }
  }
</style>
